+This method performs trilinear interpolation on a compressed sparse grid using a links array to map voxel indices to compressed value indices, handling boundary checks via masking or a zero-value hack [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [3D Trilinear Interpolation](2613-3d-trilinear-interpolation.md) by adding a link lookup step that translates grid coordinates to compressed indices while retaining the regular 8-corner neighborhood structure. Compared to nearest neighbor interpolation, it provides more precise and sharper renderings when applying multidimensional transfer functions [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs:**
-- `xyz`: Array of sample coordinates, shape `(N, 3)`, in the same coordinate system as the grid [S1, unofficial].
-- `links`: 3D integer array, shape `(Dx, Dy, Dz)`, mapping each voxel corner to an index in the compressed value array [S1, unofficial]. Invalid links are represented by negative integers [S1, unofficial].
-- `values_compressed`: Array of values, shape `(M, C)`, where `M` is the number of valid compressed entries and `C` is the channel dimension [S1, unofficial].
